'''ammoniuret''' (am-ọ̄-nī′ụ̄-ret), ''n.'' [< ''ammonia'' + ''-uret.''] In ''chem.'', one of certain supposed compounds of ammonia and a pure metal, or an oxid of a metal.

'''ammoniureted, ammoniuretted''' (am-ō-nī′ū-ret-ed), ''a.'' [< ''ammoniuret.''] Combined with ammonia or ammonium.

'''ammonoid''' (am′ọ̄-noid), ''n.'' One of the ''Ammonoidea.''

'''Ammonoidea''' (am-ọ̄-noi′dẹ̄-ä), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < ''Ammonea'' + ''-oidea.''] An ordinal name applied by some authors to the ''Ammonea.''

'''Ammophila''' (a-mof′i-lä), ''n.'' [NL., fem. of ''ammophilus'': see ''ammophilous.''] '''1.''' A small genus of grasses growing on the sandy shores of Europe and North America; the sea-reed. {{smaller|''A. arundinacea'' (common marum, sea-reed, matweed, or sea-bent) grows on sandy sea-shores, and is extensively employed in Europe and America for preserving the shores}}

